\f0\fs24 HUM.org SQL login system\par
\par
This website build is a local lab login desk. Accounts live in SQLite. PHP pages and the Python server share one schema and one password hash format.\par
\par
\b File types that matter\b0\par
SQL — schema.sql creates users, sessions, login_attempts, and csrf_tokens.\par
PHP — public forms plus includes for PDO, CSRF, and layout.\par
HTML / XHTML — landing page and a well-formed operator spec.\par
XML — auth-config.xml, sitemap.xml, and the session status API.\par
CSS / JS — theme and client-side field checks. The server still validates.\par
PY — init_auth_db.py and login_server.py for hosts without PHP.\par
RTF / DOC — these operator notes.\par
\par
\b Start the Python server\b0\par
\f1 python3 site/login/tools/init_auth_db.py init\par
python3 site/login/tools/init_auth_db.py seed --password LabOnly1234\par
python3 site/login/tools/login_server.py --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8088\f0\par
\par
Do not commit a real password. Seed only on the machine that will run the desk.\par
